WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.914
In 1926, the National Revolutionary Army began the Northern Expedition.

00:00:03.914 --> 00:00:06.819
They hoped to end the division among warlords.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:10.556
The young officers received rigorous training.

00:00:10.556 --> 00:00:14.523
The army marched north, through mountains and rivers.

00:00:14.523 --> 00:00:17.844
Along the way, many warlord forces were defeated one after another.

00:00:17.844 --> 00:00:21.855
Students and workers also promoted the ideals of the Northern Expedition.

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:25.307
People stood by the roadside, welcoming the army's arrival.

00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:29.459
With war in the distance, people longed for unification.

00:00:29.459 --> 00:00:33.170
In 1928, the Northern Expedition was largely completed.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:36.407
The National Government achieved unification in name.

00:00:36.407 --> 00:00:40.376
On Beijing's city walls, a new flag was raised.

00:00:40.376 --> 00:00:43.788
However, local conflicts still remained.

00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:46.575
Complete stability had not yet truly arrived.

00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:50.165
People hoped this was the beginning of peace.

00:00:50.165 --> 00:00:53.167
Unification brought new hope and construction.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:56.071
Railways reopened, and cities slowly recovered.
